.Dd August 28, 2026
.Dt BRFSCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm brfsctl
.Nd BrFS operator utility
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm stats
.Nm
.Cm status | peers | backlog | journal | resync
.Nm
.Cm conflicts Cm list
.Nm
.Cm conflicts Cm restore Ar name
.Nm
.Cm conflicts Cm prune Op Ar substr
.Nm
.Cm massdelete Op Cm resume
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is the operator surface of BrFS.
The
.Cm stats
command reads the
.Va security.brfs.*
kernel counters directly and works without a running daemon; every other
command talks to the
.Xr brfsd 8
control socket
.Pa /var/run/brfsd.sock ,
which is mode 0600, so run these as root (e.g. via doas).
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "conflicts restore name"
.It Cm stats
Show kernel-module counters: enabled state, total events, ring drops,
ring size.
Works with no daemon running (the kernel module is the source).
.It Cm status
Node state: node_id, primary/resynced flags, tree and state_dir paths,
content-set counts (live records and tombstones), sequence counters,
in-flight fetches, and the mass-delete guard state.
.It Cm peers
Mesh peers: node id, connection state, direction, address, write-buffer
depth.
.It Cm backlog
Queue depths: pending journal entries, incoming fetches, completion
queue.
.It Cm journal
Journal statistics: pending entries, renames in flight, echo markers,
high water sequence.
.It Cm resync
Send RESYNC_REQ to every ready peer and schedule a local rescan.
Use after freeing disk space (a fetch aborted by
.Er ENOSPC
is not retried automatically) or to force convergence.
.It Cm conflicts Cm list
List quarantined files (conflict losers) under
.Pa state_dir/conflicts/ .
.It Cm conflicts Cm restore Ar name
Move a quarantined file back into the tree (strips the timestamp suffix);
it rejoins as fresh local content and is announced.
.It Cm conflicts Cm prune Op Ar substr
Delete quarantined entries: all of them, or those whose names contain
.Ar substr .
.It Cm massdelete
Show the mass-delete guard state (clear or latched, current window
count).
.It Cm massdelete Cm resume
Release a latched mass-delete guard and schedule a rescan.
The deletes suppressed by the guard are re-derived as honest tombstones:
an intentional bulk delete still converges mesh-wide, one operator
confirmation later.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr brfs 4 ,
.Xr brfs.conf 5 ,
.Xr brfsd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in the BrFS POC in August 2026.
